WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.234
President Volodymyr Zelensky

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:03.536
says Ukraine needs long range missiles

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:06.006
following a barrage of attacks by Russia.

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:07.874
And a Ukrainian

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:09.142
diplomat says that Western

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:10.443
allies are going to be sending more

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:12.612
than 300 tanks to Ukraine.

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:13.346
Let's get

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:13.813
you updated

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:14.581
on all of this

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:15.482
with CNN senior

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:16.616
international correspondent

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:17.684
Fred Pleitgen.

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:20.286
He's live for us in Kramatorsk. Fred.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:21.921
Ukraine says that it is

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:23.857
in a race against time

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:26.192
to get these additional weapons.

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:27.160
Bring us up to speed.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.461
What's the latest

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:30.930
Well,

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.132
certainly from the vantage point here,

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:32.899
it seems as

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:33.566
though they possibly

00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:34.567
are in a race against time.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:35.702
If you look at the area around

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:37.137
where I am in the east of the country,

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:37.737
where certainly

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:39.072
right now Boris

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:40.607
The bulk of the heavy

00:00:40.607 --> 00:00:41.741
fighting is going on.

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:43.743
And we have had some rocket attacks

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:45.245
by the Russians in villages

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:46.913
not far from where I am right now.

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:47.313
And, of course,

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:48.748
you have that main battlefront

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:51.051
right now in the town of Bakhmut

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:52.018
And when the Ukrainians say

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:53.053
they're in a race against time,

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:53.753
they obviously meet

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:54.154
that they need

00:00:54.154 --> 00:00:55.422
those main battle

00:00:55.422 --> 00:00:57.490
tanks from the west as fast as possible.

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:58.658
And if you look at the battles

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:01.194
that are going on here in the east, tanks

00:01:01.194 --> 00:01:02.462
play a major role,

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:04.464
both in their classic role

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:06.266
of conducting attacks, for instance,

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:06.733
but also

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:08.535
when they're being used as artillery

00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:09.602
but when it comes to fighting

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:10.403
around cities.

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:12.272
We visited a tank unit here

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:13.606
in one of the hardest hit areas

00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:14.974
by the war around Bakhmut.

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:15.675
Here's what we saw

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:19.446
Grabbing like a

00:01:19.446 --> 00:01:20.313
dragster, the

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:22.582
crew from the 28th mechanized brigade

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:23.750
warm up their Soviet

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:26.886
era t 60 44 battle suburban

00:01:27.053 --> 00:01:28.154
some of the have problems

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:30.023
with ammunition were running low.

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:31.257
The commander tells me.

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:32.892
And that's the only problem we have

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:34.327
we get enough spare parts.

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:35.295
Our commanders work

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:36.096
all the time

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:38.131
to sustain the tank and repair it.

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:42.268
That commander who goes by the callsign

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:43.770
David raises

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:45.171
the 40 year old beast

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:46.606
towards the front line

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.475
like a steam engine train.

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:49.342
A lot of Ukraine's

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:51.845
main battle tanks are as old as this one.

00:01:51.878 --> 00:01:52.312
That's why

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:54.247
the military says they urgently need

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:56.249
those new Western main battle tanks.

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:58.118
They say around three to 400

00:01:58.118 --> 00:02:01.721
to try and turn the tide in this war.

00:02:01.721 --> 00:02:02.455
The problem,

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:04.457
Ukraine is running out of Soviet

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:05.191
era tanks

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:06.192
and is having increasing

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:08.561
trouble replacing those lost in battle

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:10.296
or needing repair.

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:11.264
The 28th helped

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:12.999
liberate their son in the south

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:14.934
and then was sent here.

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:15.502
It's already been

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:17.036
a long war for this unit.

00:02:18.071 --> 00:02:19.772
Ukrainian soldiers on the front around

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.207
Mahmoud are elated.

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:22.675
Western nations are sending

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:24.210
modern battle tanks

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:26.412
and one A to Abrams from the U.S..

00:02:26.713 --> 00:02:27.413
German made

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:30.383
leopard twos and British Challenger tanks

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:34.354
but the Ukrainians

00:02:34.354 --> 00:02:35.455
are also masters

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:37.490
at using the old Soviet tanks.

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:39.359
They have now to best effect

00:02:39.359 --> 00:02:42.195
three firing, reloading

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:45.598
taking aim and quickly

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:47.700
still shooting again.

00:02:49.269 --> 00:02:50.270
The tank engineer

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:51.571
who only gave his name is

00:02:51.571 --> 00:02:52.238
Maxim

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:53.072
says the soldiers

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:53.907
from the 28th

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:56.476
could operate these vehicles blindfolded.

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:57.810
Let's just lay down.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.546
If we fire from a covered position,

00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:01.214
we lose this device, he says.

00:03:01.214 --> 00:03:02.916
It's old and analog,

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:05.952
but pretty efficient, very precise.

00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:07.053
Ukraine's forces say

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:09.122
their tanks have been extremely important

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:11.024
and effective here in Bakhmut.

00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:12.325
Taking on the mercenaries

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:13.593
of Russia's Wagner

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:15.428
private military company,

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:17.730
who often use convicts as cannon fodder

00:03:17.931 --> 00:03:18.998
to try and storm

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:20.133
Ukrainian positions

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:22.402
with almost no fire support

00:03:22.402 --> 00:03:22.835
The tank

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:24.537
commander says they're constantly

00:03:24.537 --> 00:03:26.206
working to stop Wagner's

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:26.940
advances here,

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:28.775
but just fight against them.

00:03:28.775 --> 00:03:29.709
If we stop,

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:30.810
they will come closer

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.979
and we will lose our houses and families.

00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:34.981
We stand here to allow people

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:36.883
to peacefully live in their homes.

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:39.552
But Ukraine's army is under growing

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:40.853
pressure around Bakhmut

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:42.722
as the Russians pour more armor

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:43.990
into this area.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:45.725
The promised Western tanks

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:46.926
probably won't arrive

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:47.560
fast enough

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:50.129
to make a difference in this battle.

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:51.331
But these soldiers hope

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:53.633
they will turn the tide of the war

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:57.604
so you can see, guys, that

00:03:57.604 --> 00:03:58.605
the Ukrainians obviously

00:03:58.605 --> 00:04:00.173
saying they need a lot of those Western

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:00.873
main battle tanks.

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:01.608
And they do think

00:04:01.608 --> 00:04:03.176
that that will make a big difference

00:04:03.176 --> 00:04:04.077
on the battlefield,

00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:05.411
especially if they want to take the fight

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:05.945
to the Russians

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:06.346
and win back

00:04:06.346 --> 00:04:07.680
some of those territories

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:08.548
that the Russians

00:04:08.548 --> 00:04:09.916
got at the beginning of this war.

00:04:09.916 --> 00:04:10.650
The other thing, of course,

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:11.851
as you guys mentioned,

00:04:11.851 --> 00:04:12.518
is those longer

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:14.220
distance missiles, those attackers

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.189
that the Ukrainians also want to have.

00:04:16.189 --> 00:04:17.523
They see the main reason for that

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:18.091
is that after

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:19.559
they got the multiple rocket launchers

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:20.193
from the US,

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:20.994
they were able to hit

00:04:20.994 --> 00:04:22.662
some supply lines from the Russians,

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:23.830
take some of those out.

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:24.430
But they say now

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:25.498
the Russians have simply move

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:26.432
those supply lines

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:27.967
further away from the front line.

00:04:27.967 --> 00:04:29.535
So the Ukrainians say they need longer

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:30.870
distance capabilities

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.071
to be able to hit those as well,

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:32.672
of course.

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:34.407
We know that the Biden administration

00:04:34.407 --> 00:04:35.174
so far

00:04:35.174 --> 00:04:36.943
is not willing to give those missiles

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:37.377
just yet.

00:04:37.377 --> 00:04:38.144
The leopard tanks

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:39.879
will probably get there from the Germans

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:40.813
and from there.

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:41.414
Our European

00:04:41.414 --> 00:04:43.249
allies and partners will get there

00:04:43.249 --> 00:04:45.451
in relatively short order,

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:46.352
probably in time

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:48.655
to help them in the spring and summer.

00:04:48.855 --> 00:04:50.123
The American tanks,

00:04:50.123 --> 00:04:51.624
the Abrams will take a little bit

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:52.091
more time.

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:53.259
It will take many months before they

00:04:53.259 --> 00:04:54.160
can get on the ground

00:04:56.029 --> 00:04:58.031
Joining us now is CNN military analyst

00:04:58.031 --> 00:04:58.931
Colonel Cedric Leighton.

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:00.600
So Colonel Leighton, German

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:01.834
leopard tanks could be there

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:03.102
relatively soon.

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:03.603
As you heard

00:05:03.603 --> 00:05:04.837
there, though, from John Kirby,

00:05:04.837 --> 00:05:06.272
the Abrams tanks it could take a while.

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:08.174
Are they going to get there too late?

00:05:08.174 --> 00:05:09.642
Well, it really depends, Pamela.

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:10.043
And, you know,

00:05:10.043 --> 00:05:11.311
when you look at the difference,

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:12.745
first of all,

00:05:12.745 --> 00:05:15.448
they've talked about 321 tanks

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:17.083
according to the Ukrainian ambassador

00:05:17.083 --> 00:05:19.952
to France, being sent to Ukraine.

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:21.120
So that's a large number.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:21.854
That is basically

00:05:21.854 --> 00:05:23.289
what the Ukrainians asked for.

00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:25.391
They asked for around 300 to 400 tanks

00:05:25.391 --> 00:05:26.959
So they're getting what they need.

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:28.261
But let's take a look

00:05:28.261 --> 00:05:29.095
at the leopard tank.

00:05:29.095 --> 00:05:31.097
So this is the German leopard tank,

00:05:31.097 --> 00:05:32.732
very capable tank.

00:05:32.732 --> 00:05:35.702
It has a 120 millimeter

00:05:36.035 --> 00:05:37.470
cannon that's associated with it,

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:38.671
just like the Abrams does.

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:39.772
Good armor

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:40.773
can be used

00:05:40.773 --> 00:05:42.408
in a lot of different environments,

00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:43.676
very maneuverable.

00:05:43.676 --> 00:05:45.712
And it has a lot of firepower

00:05:45.712 --> 00:05:46.946
along with it.

00:05:46.946 --> 00:05:49.382
But it has less required training time

00:05:49.582 --> 00:05:51.084
than the Abrams tank does

00:05:51.084 --> 00:05:52.385
and the Abrams tank that you see

00:05:52.385 --> 00:05:53.553
right there.

00:05:53.553 --> 00:05:55.655
That is one that is extremely powerful.

00:05:55.655 --> 00:05:57.156
It is basically the top of the line

00:05:57.156 --> 00:05:59.559
armored vehicle that the U.S.

00:05:59.559 --> 00:06:01.494
uses for

00:06:01.494 --> 00:06:02.662
these kinds of purposes,

00:06:02.662 --> 00:06:04.063
highly maneuverable.

00:06:04.063 --> 00:06:06.232
But it does require a lot of maintenance

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:08.201
and a huge logistics tail in this case.

00:06:08.201 --> 00:06:09.335
And an adviser to President

00:06:09.335 --> 00:06:11.371
Zelensky says Ukraine is negotiating

00:06:11.571 --> 00:06:13.206
with Western allies

00:06:13.206 --> 00:06:14.941
to access long range

00:06:14.941 --> 00:06:16.175
missiles and aircrafts.

00:06:16.175 --> 00:06:17.543
How would that help change the war?

00:06:17.543 --> 00:06:19.278
And do you see this dynamic continue

00:06:19.278 --> 00:06:20.646
to play out where they get something

00:06:20.646 --> 00:06:21.347
and they say, okay,

00:06:21.347 --> 00:06:21.748
well, here's

00:06:21.748 --> 00:06:22.849
what's next on our wish list?

00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:23.116
Yeah.

00:06:23.116 --> 00:06:24.283
So there are a lot of different things

00:06:24.283 --> 00:06:25.451
that they could potentially get.

00:06:25.451 --> 00:06:27.420
So you take a look at the attack

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:28.921
system, for example.

00:06:28.921 --> 00:06:29.689
This is a system

00:06:29.689 --> 00:06:32.558
that has about 190 mile range,

00:06:32.759 --> 00:06:34.627
and it can really affect

00:06:34.627 --> 00:06:36.062
a longer range area.

00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:37.997
So it's considered a short range system,

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:40.166
but its long range enough that it would,

00:06:40.166 --> 00:06:42.301
for example, go after Crimean targets.

00:06:42.702 --> 00:06:44.070
So if the Ukrainians want to go

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:45.138
after Crimea,

00:06:45.138 --> 00:06:46.606
this is one thing that they would do

00:06:46.606 --> 00:06:49.008
there. Now, in the fighter jet world.

00:06:49.175 --> 00:06:50.276
This is an F-16

00:06:50.276 --> 00:06:51.544
courtesy of the Danish Air Force

00:06:51.544 --> 00:06:53.146
in this particular case.

00:06:53.146 --> 00:06:56.282
But what it can do is it can move around

00:06:56.549 --> 00:06:57.750
very maneuverable.

00:06:57.750 --> 00:06:58.951
It is a, you know,

00:06:58.951 --> 00:07:00.052
the top of the line aircraft,

00:07:00.052 --> 00:07:01.988
although it's almost 50 years old.

00:07:01.988 --> 00:07:04.357
First flight was about 49 years ago.

00:07:04.891 --> 00:07:07.059
These aircraft are really the mainstay

00:07:07.059 --> 00:07:08.494
or have been until recently

00:07:08.494 --> 00:07:10.563
the mainstay of the U.S. Air Force.

00:07:10.563 --> 00:07:12.532
And there it's a real big part

00:07:12.532 --> 00:07:13.933
of the data inventory.

00:07:13.933 --> 00:07:14.867
And that's something

00:07:14.867 --> 00:07:15.701
that they would require

00:07:15.701 --> 00:07:17.136
a lot of training on.

00:07:17.136 --> 00:07:18.137
Anywhere, depending

00:07:18.137 --> 00:07:19.405
on the experience of the pilot,

00:07:19.405 --> 00:07:21.374
anywhere from three months.

00:07:21.374 --> 00:07:22.742
That's a real bare minimum

00:07:22.742 --> 00:07:23.810
highly unlikely

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:25.845
all the way to a year or more.

00:07:25.845 --> 00:07:27.380
So with this training pipeline

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:28.514
for all of these systems

00:07:28.514 --> 00:07:30.082
is going to be a very long one.

00:07:30.082 --> 00:07:31.617
A very tough one.

00:07:31.617 --> 00:07:32.218
Kim Jong un

00:07:32.218 --> 00:07:34.587
sister is weighing in on all of this

00:07:34.587 --> 00:07:35.822
and she is denouncing

00:07:35.822 --> 00:07:36.722
the Western decision

00:07:36.722 --> 00:07:38.324
to send takes to Ukraine.

00:07:38.324 --> 00:07:40.493
She says the people of North Korea,

00:07:40.493 --> 00:07:43.029
North Korea, will always stand with

00:07:43.029 --> 00:07:44.163
Russia, quote, always

00:07:44.163 --> 00:07:46.299
standing in the same trench as Russia.

00:07:46.332 --> 00:07:47.867
Where do you see the war going next?

00:07:47.867 --> 00:07:49.869
So when it comes to the war,

00:07:49.902 --> 00:07:50.269
that's

00:07:50.269 --> 00:07:51.838
going to be a really interesting thing.

00:07:51.838 --> 00:07:54.240
So when you look at what you have here

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:55.007
on the main map,

00:07:55.007 --> 00:07:57.143
you have the possibility of the Russians

00:07:57.143 --> 00:08:00.580
coming in not only from the east,

00:08:00.813 --> 00:08:03.149
but also potentially from the south

00:08:03.349 --> 00:08:04.817
going into these directions.

00:08:04.817 --> 00:08:05.785
That's what they want to do.

00:08:05.785 --> 00:08:07.353
So if you go to a more detailed

00:08:07.353 --> 00:08:09.589
map of the eastern front, for example,

00:08:09.589 --> 00:08:10.356
the big fighting

00:08:10.356 --> 00:08:11.190
that you have around

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:13.459
solider around bombed,

00:08:13.459 --> 00:08:15.661
all those areas here become

00:08:16.295 --> 00:08:19.165
that becomes a symbol for what

00:08:19.398 --> 00:08:20.800
the Russians want to do now.

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:21.334
By itself

00:08:21.334 --> 00:08:23.369
is not very strategically significant.

00:08:23.369 --> 00:08:25.238
However, it is on our main highway

00:08:25.238 --> 00:08:26.472
that goes this way.

00:08:26.472 --> 00:08:28.274
And if they can use that highway,

00:08:28.274 --> 00:08:30.009
that could potentially be a gateway

00:08:30.009 --> 00:08:30.710
for the Russians

00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:31.711
to move

00:08:31.911 --> 00:08:32.912
forward into

00:08:32.912 --> 00:08:34.814
Ukrainian controlled territory.

00:08:34.814 --> 00:08:37.149
But they are going to, in essence,

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:38.918
try to work around a stalemate.

00:08:38.918 --> 00:08:40.353
The Ukrainians are trying to run

00:08:40.353 --> 00:08:41.153
the clock out

00:08:41.153 --> 00:08:42.054
They're trying to make it

00:08:42.054 --> 00:08:43.556
so that they can fight the Russians

00:08:43.556 --> 00:08:45.057
and at the very least, keep them here.

00:08:45.057 --> 00:08:46.192
But their real goal

00:08:46.192 --> 00:08:48.427
is to eliminate the Russians

00:08:48.628 --> 00:08:49.395
from this part

00:08:49.395 --> 00:08:51.130
right here, the so-called land bridge

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:53.132
That is where the Ukrainians want to move

00:08:53.132 --> 00:08:54.667
in the opposite direction

00:08:54.667 --> 00:08:57.570
and bring the Russians in this way

00:08:57.737 --> 00:08:59.672
and to force them out of the country.

00:08:59.672 --> 00:09:00.106
All right.

00:09:00.106 --> 00:09:00.806
Really interesting

00:09:00.806 --> 00:09:02.074
Thank you so much, Colonel

